cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AirDB.jl in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "AirDB.jl: a PostgreSQL-backed persistence layer for Air.jl"
abstract: >-
  AirDB.jl keeps shared application state in memory as immutable forms and
  persists every committed change to PostgreSQL in transaction order, using
  Air.jl's software transactional memory. It provides database-backed volatile,
  actor, promise, stream, and delay forms, a registered extern-type system for
  host-level values, owner/ACL metadata, garbage collection, and a fault-isolating
  write pipeline.
authors:
